<title>FRANCE: Canal Plus/Nethold aim for 14 mln subscribers.</title>
<headline>Canal Plus/Nethold aim for 14 mln subscribers.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new pay television group formed out of the merger of Canal Plus and Nethold hopes to have 14 million subscribers by the end of 1999, against 9.7 million currently, director Michel Thoulouze said on Friday.</p>
<p>He told a Canal Plus shareholders' meeting that the group expected the Nethold activities to reach break-even in the second half of 1999.</p>
<p>Nethold is currently owned by Richemont and MIH.</p>
